# Working on [[.Name]]

This CLI uses Loop's shared runtime. Keep project behaviour in `project.json`.
The small Go entry point embeds that file and calls the public project/CLI facade.
Do not duplicate request handling or copy runtime internals into this repository.

Load only the relevant skill:

- [Develop this CLI](.agents/skills/[[.Name]]-develop/SKILL.md): extend operations or their supporting API and verify behaviour.
- [Test this CLI](.agents/skills/[[.Name]]-test/SKILL.md): verify command contracts and debug integration failures.
- [Prepare a release](.agents/skills/[[.Name]]-release/SKILL.md): discover existing distribution infrastructure and configure publishing.

Use `go mod tidy`, then `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` before shipping.
The fixture tests use a local HTTP server, never the configured real API.
Keep `go.sum` under version control after dependency resolution.
Never put credential values in the manifest, source, tests or release configuration.
The endpoint in the initial manifest is an example. Adapt it and its contract test
to the project's actual admin API before treating the CLI as production-ready.
